; comboedit.eval - EDITING a surface combination reaches every square painted
; with it, on every level, by reference (editor-updates P3).
;
; tools/EditorTest.py writes, before this runs (and restores the project after):
;   [marble_hall]  floor = floor_slabs floor_rubble   wall = wall_marble
;                  ceiling = ceiling_stone
;
; 1. crypt2 is painted with it whole and saved; the party goes back to
;    eval_arena, whose room A is painted with it too. crypt2 is now a level
;    NOT loaded that uses the combination; crypt1 is one that does not.
; 2. The type editor's Save (typeset) changes the floor to floor_temple:
;    room A's squares show floor_temple at once, crypt2's do once visited,
;    and the save that follows writes crypt2 (stashed, it uses it) but NOT
;    crypt1 (asked through its read-only copy, and left alone).
; 3. A rename reaches the squares; a delete is refused while any use it.
; 4. Renaming a FLOOR TYPE that is a member keeps the combination resolving.

logecho on
reset
echo --- 1: crypt2 painted whole ---
goto crypt2
editor fill combos marble_hall level
editor cell 5 5
savemap
goto eval_arena
editor fill walls wall_marble rect 8 1 26 22
editor fill combos marble_hall area 3 3
editor cell 3 3
editor cell 7 22
geomhash
echo --- 2: the floor redefined ---
typeset combos marble_hall floor floor_temple
editor cell 3 3
editor cell 7 22
geomhash
savemap
goto crypt2
editor cell 5 5
goto eval_arena
echo --- 3: renamed ---
typeset rename combos marble_hall grand_hall
editor cell 3 3
typerefs combos grand_hall
typeset delete combos grand_hall
echo --- 4: a member type renamed ---
typeset rename floors floor_temple floor_temple_b
editor cell 3 3
